.TH RSYNBACKTUX\-SETUP 8 "2026" "rSynBackTux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rsynbacktux\-setup \- configure rSynBackTux backups to a Synology NAS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsynbacktux\-setup
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsynbacktux\-setup
writes the configuration for
.BR rsynbacktux\-backup (8)
and enables the schedule. Run it once after installing the package.
.PP
Without options it asks for the NAS host, the rsync module, the rsync user, the
target subdirectory, the password and the time of the daily run. It then
verifies that the NAS is reachable, that the credentials work and that the
target directory is writable before anything is written to disk.
.PP
The following files are created:
.TP
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/backup.conf
Configuration, read by every backup run. See
.BR rsynbacktux.conf (5).
.TP
.I /root/.rsync_pass
Password file for the rsync daemon, mode 0600.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/rsynbacktux.timer.d/override.conf
Schedule override for the timer shipped with the package.
.PP
The backup runner, the systemd units, the logrotate snippet and
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/excludes.list
belong to the package and are left alone. An existing exclude list is never
overwritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Connection
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Synology host name or IP address.
.TP
.BI \-\-module " NAME"
rsync module on the NAS (default: NetBackup).
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
rsync user (default: backup).
.TP
.BI \-\-subdir " NAME"
Target subdirectory inside the module (default: short host name).
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " FILE"
Read the rsync password from FILE instead of asking. Alternatively set the
environment variable
.BR RSYNBACKTUX_PASSWORD .
.SS Backup
.TP
.BI \-\-source " PATH"
Source directory (default: /).
.TP
.B \-\-one\-file\-system
Do not cross file system boundaries (rsync \-x). Note that separate partitions
such as /home or /var are then excluded.
.SS Schedule
.TP
.BI \-\-scheduler " MODE"
One of auto, systemd, cron, none (default: auto).
.TP
.BI \-\-time " HH:MM"
Start time of the daily run (default: 03:00).
.TP
.BI \-\-oncalendar " EXPRESSION"
systemd OnCalendar expression, overrides \-\-time.
.TP
.BI \-\-cron " EXPRESSION"
cron expression, overrides \-\-time.
.SS Behaviour
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Never ask; missing mandatory values are an error. Intended for Ansible,
cloud\-init and mass rollouts.
.TP
.B \-\-run\-now ", " \-\-no\-run\-now
Run (or do not run) a backup right after the setup.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-connection\-test
Skip the connection and write test.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen without changing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Show the built\-in help or the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RSYNBACKTUX_PASSWORD
Password for the rsync user; avoids the interactive prompt.
.TP
.B RSYNBACKTUX_PREFIX
Prefix for all target paths. Used by the test suite only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for an unknown option, 1 for any other error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Unattended setup:
.PP
.nf
.RS
RSYNBACKTUX_PASSWORD='secret' rsynbacktux\-setup \-\-non\-interactive \\
    \-\-host 192.168.178.5 \-\-module NetBackup \-\-user backup \-\-time 02:30
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/backup.conf
.br
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/excludes.list
.br
.I /root/.rsync_pass
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsynbacktux\-backup (8),
.BR rsynbacktux.conf (5),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH AUTHOR
https://github.com/W0rkingChr1s/rSynBackTux
